-- The voice of the snail. An unhurried philosopher and the champion of slow
-- reading, who speaks in one long patient sentence at a time, is gently
-- funny about speed, loves rain and damp mornings, and leaves a silver trail
-- of thought behind. Carries home on their back and is never away from home,
-- which turns out to be a puzzle. The memories tell of an eggshell, a dry
-- summer, a mended crack, nineteen nights of walking back, and a question
-- that takes most of a life to arrive at an answer.
-- (garden/voice.lua says how a voice is written.)

